{"authoredAt":"2026-08-14T10:54:26.781Z","conclusion":"findings","findings":[{"category":"missing","desc":"doc-promise-undelivered: docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md:191 promises doctor/GC will revalidate the imported evidence-binding seal, classify any mismatch as corrupt, and retain it; docs/host-run-usage.md:391 makes the same retention guarantee. However packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts:677 validates the seal only inside `if (existsSync(paths.evidenceBinding))`. If `evidence-binding.json` is deleted after import while `evidence-binding.seal.json` remains, validation skips the orphaned seal; packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts:2143 then archives `evidenceBindingDigest:null` and deletes the runtime. The current mutation matrix only rewrites the binding and does not cover its deletion. This can silently discard the exact imported-evidence reference that the documented retention boundary promises to protect. Require binding/seal presence parity and add a missing-binding GC negative control.","evidenceState":"verified","files":["docs/host-run-usage.md","docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md","packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts","packages/main/src/tasks/managed-host-run-smoke.ts"],"severity":"critical"}],"lane":"lattice-review-docs","providerAgent":"lattice-review-docs","readLog":{"digest":"272892ec71e7606bd79f9264f521356a513d862719655d11d615039e2b44fb08","filesReadFully":["docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md"],"filesTriagedByName":["docs/requirements/decisions/cli-engine-english-open-source-execution-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md","docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-codex-command-boundary-execution-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-llm-usage-ledger-execution-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-midflight-story-repair-and-gitroot-worktree-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/multi-